WordNet base layer (data/wordnet/extract/, src/wordnet.ts)
---------------------------------------------------------------
The WordNet extract in this repository is derived from the

  Open English WordNet 2024
  © Global WordNet Association and the Open English WordNet contributors

licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License
(CC BY 4.0): https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Source: https://en-word.net/ (WNDB-format release, english-wordnet-2024).
The extract is a trimmed, re-encoded subset (synsets for nouns, verbs and
adjectives with their glosses; hypernym, meronym, antonym, similar-to,
entailment and causation relations). It was produced by
scripts/import-wordnet.py; see that script and docs/design-base-nets-and-chat.md
for exactly what was kept and what was trimmed.

Open English WordNet is itself derived from Princeton WordNet:

  WordNet 3.1 © 2011 Princeton University
  https://wordnet.princeton.edu — used under the WordNet License
  (BSD-style, permissive): https://wordnet.princeton.edu/license-and-commercial-use

FrameNet base layer (installed locally by scripts/import-framenet.py)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
The FrameNet layer is NOT shipped in this repository: it is installed on
demand by scripts/import-framenet.py (the bundle it writes to
data/framenet/ and the raw download under data/raw/ are gitignored; a
small fixture subset for tests lives in test/fixtures/framenet/). The
data installed is

  FrameNet Release 1.5
  © The Regents of the University of California / International
    Computer Science Institute (ICSI), Berkeley
  https://framenet.icsi.berkeley.edu

licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 License (CC BY 3.0):
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/ — FrameNet has been offered
under this Attribution-only license since Release 1.5 (see the release
notes and docs/design-base-nets-and-chat.md §3.3), which permits
modification, bundling and commercial use with attribution.

Source used by the installer: the NLTK project's public mirror of the
release (nltk_data GitHub repository, packages/corpora/framenet_v15.zip).
The full frame inventory is imported untrimmed (1,019 frames, 9,634
frame elements, 11,942 lexical units, 1,676 frame relations); the
annotated-sentence corpus is not imported. Lemma-to-WordNet-synset
linkage in the installed layer is AnSci's own bridge work, not FrameNet
data.

CSKG spike layer (loaded locally from data/raw/cskg/, src/cskg/)
----------------------------------------------------------------
The CSKG data is NOT shipped in this repository: the files under
data/raw/cskg/ are gitignored local downloads. The src/cskg/ package is
a self-contained spike (2026-11-09) that loads

  CSKG: The CommonSense Knowledge Graph
  Ilievski, Szekely & Zhang, ESWC 2021
  USC Information Sciences Institute
  https://github.com/usc-isi-i2/cskg — data: Zenodo record 4331372

CSKG unifies ConceptNet, WordNet, FrameNet, ATOMIC, Roget's Thesaurus,
a Wikidata subset and Visual Genome. Its distributors offer it under
the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International License
(CC BY-SA 4.0) per the project documentation; the Zenodo record lists
CC BY 4.0. AnSci treats it as CC BY-SA 4.0. The component sources keep
their own terms (see the CSKG documentation); the loader preserves each
edge's source dataset so provenance survives into the chat's answers.

Everything else in this repository — the ontology graph, seed data, reasoner
and chat — is original AnSci work (see README.md). ConceptNet is a planned
base net (design doc §4) and is not yet bundled; when it lands, its
attribution will be added here.
